  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "0nkgmoncfv0iGuzY4k+VvgUAVQk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:38:31.016Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`RemoteDocumentController` composes a `PHDocumentController` and adds remote push/pull over GraphQL \u2014 for callers who want to create or edit documents and sync them to a reactor server **without** setting up a full `ReactorClient` (PGlite, job queue and the rest). It works with any controller from `PHDocumentController.forDocumentModel()`, and its action methods are type-safe and chainable.\n\nTwo modes:\n\n**Batch.** Actions accumulate locally; `status.pendingActionCount` reports how many are waiting, and `push()` sends them in a **single `MutateDocument` call**.\n\n```ts\ncontroller.setName({ name: \"A\" });\ncontroller.setName({ name: \"B\" });   // pendingActionCount === 2\nawait controller.push();             // one mutation\n```\n\n**Streaming.** Actions are pushed automatically after each synchronous chain via `queueMicrotask`, so everything in one chain \u2014 one microtask \u2014 is **coalesced into a single push**. If a push fails, the actions stay in the tracker and are retried on the next action; `onPushError` is the reporting hook.\n\nCreating a document is the same call with `documentId: \"\"` plus a `parentIdentifier` naming the drive; pulling an existing one passes its id.\n\nNote the standing on this class: ADR 0002 catalogued its structural limits \u2014 no persistence, no offline model, no shared cache, imperative and non-reactive, and a reimplementation of sync on weaker primitives \u2014 and folded its responsibilities into `GraphQLReactorClient.execute`. It remains the documented low-level path.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/reactor-browser/src/remote-controller/README.md` \u2014 Overview; Quick Start; Modes \u203a Batch mode and Streaming mode\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:38:31.016Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:38:31.016Z"
    }
  },
